INT. FLOODED SUBWAY TUNNEL - NIGHT

Black water to the knees. Emergency lights flicker amber on slimed tiles. A stalled train lies like a dead worm along the track.

Three survivors wade toward an iron ladder: ROSARIO VEGA, thirties, nurse, carrying a child's backpack; TIMOTHY BANKS, forties, accountant, limping; BEATRIX ORLOV, seventies, retired conductor, steady as a rock.

BEATRIX
The ladder is at the next platform.

TIMOTHY
How far?

BEATRIX
Two hundred yards.

ROSARIO
He's bleeding.

BEATRIX
We all are.

Timothy grimaces. His hand is wrapped in a torn shirt. Rosario takes his arm and slings it over her shoulder. They move.

A radio crackles from Beatrix's belt.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Unit nine, unit nine. Do you copy?

Beatrix grabs it.

BEATRIX
Dispatch. We're alive. Three of us. Tunnel six.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Copy. Rescue is en route. Stay put. Ten minutes.

TIMOTHY
Ten minutes?

ROSARIO
We can wait ten.

TIMOTHY
The water's rising.

ROSARIO
It's been rising an hour.

BEATRIX
She's right. It's slowed.

They stop on a ledge above the tracks and sit in a line. For a moment there is peace. Rosario fishes a granola bar from the backpack, breaks it in three, hands out the pieces. They chew in silence.

TIMOTHY
This is nice.

BEATRIX
Don't.

TIMOTHY
What?

BEATRIX
You'll jinx it.

Rosario smiles. Timothy smiles. Beatrix doesn't.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio, urgent)
Unit nine, new report. Upstream dam is failing. Move to high ground immediately.

ROSARIO
There is no high ground.

BEATRIX
There is a ladder.

TIMOTHY
I can't climb.

ROSARIO
Yes you can.

BEATRIX ^
Yes you can.

A distant roar rolls down the tunnel, wind pushing ahead of water. The amber lights shiver. Rosario hauls Timothy upright. Beatrix is already wading.

BEATRIX (CONT'D)
Run!
